# Expected private build assets (design doc L0, incident families P3.4/P10.1).
# One entry per line: "<path relative to the package root>" optionally followed
# by a 64-hex sha256 baseline. Existence is always required; a recorded hash is
# verified when present. The artwork stays out of Git by design; this manifest
# ships in Git so every checkout can run tools/check-private-assets.py. An
# artwork-free checkout (CI shape) is green with an explicit fresh-checkout
# note; any artwork present puts the gate in strict mode, so a partial or
# drifted maintainer copy fails red at layer 0.
#
# Requirement provenance (checked against the actual tool logic):
#   working.png, wallpaper-scene-q-v3.png, scene.js
#     tools/build-macos.sh asset guard; working/wallpaper also in
#     tools/build-startup.py PRIVATE_STARTUP_INPUTS; wallpaper also in
#     tools/build-wallpaper.py.
#   app-icon/source.png, entry-avatar.png
#     theme-config.json identity.iconInput / identity.entryAvatarInput, enforced
#     by tools/build-startup.py _require_private_inputs and tools/build-preflight.py.
#   app-icon/zcode.png
#     theme-config.json hostIcons.zcode, enforced by tools/verify-artifacts.py.
